WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.769
-I want to talk about the fact
that you obviously

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.104
had a longstanding relationship
with Trump's children.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:05.538
And you mention in the book

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.374
that in the early days
of his campaign,

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:11.143
they would come to you and
ask him to get out of the race.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:14.814
They also thought that his
rhetoric early on was racist.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:20.086
Now, it does seem like they were
not repulsed on a moral level.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:24.023
They were more worried about how
it would hurt the Trump brands,

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.059
the clothing brands.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.828
What do you --
What have you observed

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:33.699
from their sort of journey
from being against his rhetoric

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:37.504
to now seeming to be very
full-throated supporters of his?

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.005
-It's really a complete 180.

00:00:40.005 --> 00:00:41.741
When they first came to me,
the three --

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.409
Don, Ivanka, and Eric
came to me.

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:47.280
This was post the initial launch
of the campaign

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.484
when he made the statements
about Mexicans.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.353
The very first reaction
by Univision was,

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:57.123
"We're pulling out
from the Trump Doral,"

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.525
and it was costing
the Trump organization,

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:03.429
between Doral and other
properties that they have,

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.999
it was costing them
tens of millions of dollars.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.068
And the kids came to me,
and they stated,

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.538
"Look, you know, you got
to get Dad to stop this.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.573
This is --
We're gonna be out of business.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.942
Very soon you'll be the CEO
of this company,"

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:19.845
and they were gonna change the
name to the Rump Organization.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:24.049
-Now, I do want to ask this
question of you right now --

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:25.651
-But it is interesting
if you look at it.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.920
Don Jr. has now become

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.823
the spokesperson
for the Second Amendment.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.926
And that's also,
I believe, included.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.495
Trump hates guns.
Right?

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:39.598
And Trump hated the fact that
Don and Eric went to Zimbabwe

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.567
and that they killed
a whole slew of animals.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.537
Could not understand how stupid
that they could be

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:48.575
to allow those photos
to end up on the Internet.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.476
That, "You know, you guys think
that you're big tough guys

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:53.646
with a $10,000 gun
that I ended up paying for,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:57.182
shooting, you know, an animal
while you're sitting there."

00:01:57.182 --> 00:02:00.253
Many of us had to go there
and explain to Mr. Trump

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.389
that they had licenses for it,
that they did it the proper way.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.992
They weren't illegally
doing anything

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:09.028
and that all of the meat
was actually provided

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:13.266
to villages
that survived off of that.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.368
He didn't care.
It didn't make a difference.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.736
He hates guns.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.839
And it's just interesting
that now Don Jr.,

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.875
who was really considered
the one child

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:26.012
who had the worst judgment
of any of his children,

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.515
somehow managed to be
front and center,

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:33.753
specifically with the NRA
and talking Trump.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.022
I mean,
it's truly an amazing thing.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.458
It's something that he's wanted
his whole life,

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:40.926
acknowledgement from his father.

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:44.329
-It does also amaze me
that maybe where Trump

00:02:44.329 --> 00:02:48.334
is most concerned about legality
is in big-game hunting.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.069
-Yeah.
-Michael, obviously,

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.839
you're aware of this,
that a lot of people --

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.473
You say it's important
to write a book like this,

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.843
because to understand
the badness of Donald Trump,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.944
you have to hear directly
from the bad guys

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.113
who worked for him and did
the bad things for him.

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:03.148
You're admitting
to serving that role.

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:08.087
Yet there are people questioning
why you should be sort of hailed

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:12.891
as an anti-Trump hero now
after everything you have done.

00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:14.327
Like, what do you say to people

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.963
who question the way
you're being perceived now?

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:20.866
-So, first of all, I've never
asked anybody to call me a hero,

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:25.271
to the same extent I never asked
anybody to call me the villain.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.107
I have to make amends
to my wife, my daughter, my son,

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.608
and to this country.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:32.745
And as I stated once
to George Stephanopoulos

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.079
several years ago,

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:37.216
my loyalty is to my family
and to this country.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:41.620
And it took me getting --
basically losing everything.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.022
I talk about this
in the epilogue

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.324
that I'm broke and I'm broken.

00:03:45.324 --> 00:03:49.728
And it took this sort of kick
to really push me

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:52.932
into acknowledging the things
that I did

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:54.967
and the loss of my moral compass

00:03:54.967 --> 00:03:59.805
for a man who lacks
a moral compass on his own.

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:03.976
Why I fell into the cult
and how I fell into the cult,

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:08.014
I really can't
describe it adequately,

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:11.984
other than to say the 38%
of this country, his base,

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.886
including members of Congress,

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.689
are doing exactly
the same thing that I did.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.991
And I'm trying to say to them,

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:22.027
from one member of the cult
to another,

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.296
open up your eyes
and acknowledge

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:27.233
that Trump doesn't care
about you,

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.668
he doesn't care about
your family,

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:31.904
he doesn't care about anything
other than winning this election

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.273
and, in essence,
becoming an autocrat,

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.909
which is what he wants to be.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:40.446
-Also in the book,
you sort of admit to personally

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.949
and sort of rabidly
pushing the birtherism,

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:47.553
um, you know, "theory,"
for lack of a better term.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.690
As we're having this sort of
national reckoning of race,

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.992
I imagine it must be painful to
acknowledge the role you served

00:04:53.992 --> 00:04:56.795
in putting a racist
in the White House.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:58.765
-Well, yes.
And one of the things

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.799
I tried to do when I created

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:03.402
the National Diversity Coalition
for Trump

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.137
was really to open up his eyes

00:05:05.137 --> 00:05:09.108
and understand
that America is not white.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:12.544
America is a multiracial,
multiethnic country.

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:13.946
We're the melting pot.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.548
And he really needs
to understand that.

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:18.951
And so
I created this organization

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.520
that really exploded in size.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.792
And we had everybody from,
you know, Jews to Christians

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:28.193
to Muslims, black, white, brown.

00:05:28.193 --> 00:05:29.796
It encompassed everybody.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.931
And my hope was that,
by seeing his crowd,

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:36.569
which is predominantly white,
and it is to this day,

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:39.839
that he would understand that if
you want to win the election,

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:42.908
you need to seek out
the minority vote.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.678
You need to understand
that America -- right? --

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:49.315
is not white and that, you know,

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.617
they are an important
voting bloc.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.553
They're important
to this country.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:57.156
And I failed in that.
I failed miserably.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:01.327
-I was surprised to read, but
also appreciated the honesty,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:04.830
that you do still
have affection for

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.467
and care for President Trump.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:10.336
-Yeah, it's -- it's hard.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:12.739
I guess the only way
to describe it is

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:17.543
the same way you have a parent
that is somewhat abusive to you,

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.446
and you still care about them.

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:25.051
But at least I recognize the
person that I'm dealing with.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:28.654
And again, all I'm just trying
to do is to make amends

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:32.458
and to allow the book
to serve as a basis

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:37.530
for people to understand --
this is the man that wants you

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.799
to vote for him
and to pull the lever

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:42.768
on his behalf come Election Day.

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:45.738
And I'm giving you all of
the inside information

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:49.208
that you need in order
to make the determination

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.644
whether this man
is really who you think

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:55.080
is best for you
and best for this country.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:58.584
-Well, Michael, I do wish you
luck in your next chapter.

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:01.453
And I want to read
just a quote from the book.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:04.356
It's really
a beautiful piece of prose.

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:05.791
And I hope
if there's anything

00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:09.261
that people take away
from the book, it's this.

00:07:09.261 --> 00:07:12.231
"Trump was fresh from the shower
and hadn't done his hair yet..."

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.267
-[ Laughs ]
-"...as it was still air-drying.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:17.336
When his hair wasn't done,
his strands of dyed golden hair

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:21.207
reached below his shoulders,
along the right side of his head

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:24.610
and on his back,
like a balding Allman brother

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.512
or strung-out old '60s hippy."

00:07:27.512 --> 00:07:31.116
Really, truly, beautiful prose.

00:07:31.116 --> 00:07:32.451
-Seth, thank you very much

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.787
for picking
that part of the book out.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:38.391
-And I do recommend, everybody,
when you buy the book,

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:40.126
just go right to
"Flip flop flap,"

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:42.461
because that is an incredible --

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:44.763
incredible explanation
of what's going on up there.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:46.432
Thank you so much
for being here, Michael.

